  "notes": "West leads the ♣9 against 4♠. West's club lead is won by South. The ♠A and ♠K are certain losers. South has a third loser in hearts. The only danger is that the defense might be able to get a club ruff.\n\nSouth should take the precaution of cashing the ♦A, ♦K, and ruffing dummy's third diamond in hand before playing trump. Should the defender who wins the first trump trick be able to give his partner a club ruff, South must hope that the defender short in clubs also has the ♥K.\n\nBy eliminating that player's safe diamond exits, South's heart loser will go away on the above layout. West can cash a spade trick, but he is then endplayed. A heart return, away from the ♥K, will do no good while a diamond return will concede a ruff and discard.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♣9 against 4♠. West's club lead is won by South. The ♠A and ♠K are certain losers. South has a third loser in hearts. The only danger is that the defense might be able to get a club ruff.",
